{
  "dom_id": "step-q133622",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/e4b568fe2226154be401a2332c718f143954d98fdbd8a0c679fdb99fcdd47d14.png)\n\nSarah interviewed some parents, asking them how much time their children spend playing outdoors per day. The information she received is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n- There is only one child aged $6$ among those surveyed.\n- None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3.5,$ namely, $(5,3.5).$ This means that only one child spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0103370189c7156f9677ca576e2480bc99314cd312702fca3ea3e50cb4f7287a.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,2)$ and $(6,2.5).$ This means that there were two children of age $6$ among those surveyed.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/0a8ca9628b48e643e1aa9e9f0216148881db237c2d29054b29f4377ad182503d.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors. Those children are represented by the two dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/4d9709c131045f2e440204f79ad3fd8ff22707312b0e99138da558393e8b7f6d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
